export const HELP_KB =
  'Lexy Recruiter Guide \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Version 1.0 • July 2026 • For recruiters, recruiter admins &\n hiring managers\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n## Contents \n \n \n- Welcome & how Lexy works \n \n- Getting started: login, roles & navigation \n \n- Dashboard & Morning Report \n \n- Work Orders (Jobs) \n \n- The Ideal Candidate Profile (ICP) \n \n- Sourcing & AI Agent Runs \n \n- The Pipeline Board (Kanban) \n \n- Candidates & the 360° Profile \n \n- Resume Screening & Verification \n \n- Outreach, Approvals & the Inbox \n \n- AI Interviews (end to end) \n \n- Recruiter Intro Videos \n \n- Evaluation Reports & Hiring-Manager Sharing \n \n- Talent Match, Rediscovery & Internal Talent \n \n- Engagement & Anti-Ghost \n \n- Analytics, Calibration & Fairness \n \n- Market Intelligence & Ask Lexy \n \n- LINX Queue (agency ↔ client collaboration) \n \n- Team, Settings & Subscription \n \n- Compliance, Privacy & Candidate Consent \n \n- Troubleshooting & FAQ \n \n- Glossary \n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 1. Welcome & how Lexy works \n \n Lexy is an AI-powered hiring platform. You stay in control of every decision; Lexy\'s team of\n AI agents does the heavy lifting: reading job descriptions, finding and scoring candidates,\n drafting outreach, running structured screening interviews, verifying profiles, and writing\n client-ready evaluation reports.\n \n \n### The agent team behind the scenes \n \n \n| \n Agent | \n What it does | \n Where you see it | \n \n \n| \n ICP Agent | \n \n Reads your job description and extracts an Ideal Candidate Profile — skills, seniority,\n certifications, disqualifiers, location.\n | \n Work Order → ICP tab | \n \n \n| \n Sourcing Agent | \n \n Searches internal talent first, then external providers, and ranks matches against the\n ICP.\n | \n Work Order → Sourcing tab, Agent Hub | \n \n \n| \n Screening Agent | \n \n Screens resumes against the role, producing a recommendation and matched/missing skills.\n | \n Candidate profile → Resume Screening | \n \n \n| \n Outreach Agent | \n \n Drafts personalized first-touch emails in your brand voice. Drafts wait for your approval\n by default.\n | \n Outreach → Pending approvals | \n \n \n| \n Conversation Agent | \n Classifies inbound replies (interested, not now, unsubscribe) and drafts responses. | \n Inbox | \n \n \n| \n Interview Agent ("Lexy") | \n \n Conducts live, voice-based structured interviews, grades every answer, and writes a\n summary.\n | \n Interview room, interview reports | \n \n \n| \n Verification Agent | \n Cross-checks candidate claims (identity, employment consistency) and raises flags. | \n Candidate profile → Verification | \n \n \n| \n Anti-Ghost Agent | \n Watches for silence and no-shows, and nudges at the right moments. | \n Anti-Ghost, Work Order → Anti-Ghost tab | \n \n \n| \n Intelligence Agent | \n Continuously accrues a multi-dimension candidate score as new evidence arrives. | \n Candidate profile → Intelligence | \n \n \n| \n Digest Agent | \n Compiles your Morning Report and daily priorities. | \n Dashboard | \n \n \n \n Golden rule Lexy proposes, you decide. Outreach requires your approval before sending,\n stage moves you make manually always win over agent gates, and every AI evaluation is\n presented as evidence for your decision — never a verdict.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 2. Getting started: login, roles & navigation \n \n### Logging in \n \n \n- Open your Lexy workspace URL in a modern browser (Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox). \n \n- \n Sign in with your work email and password, or via your company\'s Microsoft single sign-on if\n enabled.\n \n \n- \n If you don\'t have an account, ask your Recruiter Admin to invite you from Team .\n You\'ll receive an invite email with an activation link.\n \n \n \n### Roles & what each can see \n \n \n| \n Role | \n Access | \n \n \n| \n Recruiter | \n \n Works only with candidates and pipelines tied to the work orders assigned to them .\n Full workflow access on those reqs: sourcing, outreach, interviews, evaluations.\n | \n \n \n| \n Recruiter Admin | \n \n Everything a recruiter has, across the whole team, plus the Approvals queue,\n Team management (invite, edit roles), and governance/decision queues (view). Can\n manage line staff in their own tenant.\n | \n \n \n| \n Tenant Admin | \n Adds subscription/billing management and tenant-level settings. | \n \n \n| \n Hiring Manager | \n \n A focused view: dashboard, open roles, candidates awaiting their approval or interview\n feedback. Cannot trigger sourcing or change AI settings.\n | \n \n \n| \n Platform Admin | \n \n Lexy staff only: client management, platform candidate pool, system health, fairness\n dashboards.\n | \n \n \n \n Recruiter visibility is assignment-based If you can\'t find a candidate or work order\n you expect to see, check whether the req is assigned to you. Ask your Recruiter Admin to\n assign it — visibility follows assignment, by design.\n \n \n### Finding your way around \n \n \n- \n Sidebar (left, always dark): Dashboard, Work Orders, Approvals (admins), Candidates,\n Internal Talent, Sourcing, Outreach & Inbox, Engagement, Anti-Ghost, Analytics, Market\n Intel, LINX Queue, AI Job Queue, Team, Settings.\n \n \n- \n Light / dark theme : toggle in the header. The interview room always stays dark for\n candidates by design.\n \n \n- \n Scores everywhere : a score shown as — means "not evaluated yet", which\n is different from a real 0. Lexy never fakes a number.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 3. Dashboard & Morning Report \n The Dashboard is your daily home base. \n \n### Morning Report \n \n \n- \n A daily digest compiled by the Digest Agent: what happened overnight, what needs your\n attention today, and direct links ("doors") into each item.\n \n \n- \n Every count in the report matches exactly what you\'ll see when you click through — same\n filters, same compliance rules. If a count excludes erased or do-not-contact candidates, the\n report says so.\n \n \n \n### KPI cards \n \n \n- Roles in Motion — active work orders with pipeline activity. \n \n- Total Candidates — your visible bench (excludes erased/DNC records). \n \n- AI Interview Sessions — completed and in-flight structured interviews. \n \n- Hires — placements recorded via the offer funnel. \n \n \n Clicking a KPI opens the exact list behind the number — the count and the list always agree.\n \n \n### Other dashboard widgets \n \n \n- \n AI Command Center — start a sourcing run or screening task without leaving the\n dashboard.\n \n \n- Pipeline Funnel — candidate distribution across stages, clickable per stage. \n \n- \n Hire-Ready Candidates — your highest-scored, furthest-progressed people right now.\n \n \n- \n Agent Activity Feed — a real-time, truthful log of what the agents actually did (with\n real timestamps). "Agents online" reflects genuinely active runs and live interviews.\n \n \n- \n Live Run view — while a sourcing/screening run is executing, the dashboard can take\n over with the latest events streaming in; the elapsed clock stops when the run finishes.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 4. Work Orders (Jobs) \n \n A Work Order is a hiring requisition: the job, its ideal candidate profile, its pipeline, its\n interviews and its analytics — all in one workspace.\n \n \n### Creating a work order \n \n \n- Go to Work Orders → New Work Order . \n \n- \n Paste or write the job description. The richer the JD, the better the ICP the AI extracts.\n \n \n- \n Fill in title, department, location, work type (on-site / hybrid / remote — remote\n roles skip location filtering in sourcing), and compensation if known.\n \n \n- \n Optionally record your client\'s own requisition number — Lexy also assigns its own\n internal Work Order # automatically; the two are kept separate and both are searchable.\n \n \n- \n Submit. Depending on your tenant\'s policy the work order may enter Pending Approval .\n \n \n \n### The approval gate \n \n Nothing runs on an unapproved job While a work order is in pending approval ,\n draft , or rejected status, Lexy blocks all candidate actions on it: no sourcing,\n no outreach, no interview invites, no interview links — even previously issued links stop\n working. Approvers (Recruiter Admins / Hiring Managers) act from the Approvals queue.\n Once approved, everything unlocks.\n \n \n### Work order tabs \n \n \n| \n Tab | \n What you do there | \n \n \n| \n Overview | \n Status, department, assigned recruiter, aggregate stats, approval state. | \n \n \n| \n ICP | \n Review and edit the AI-extracted Ideal Candidate Profile (Section 5). | \n \n \n| \n Sourcing | \n Trigger agent runs, review sourced matches, opt in to platform recommendations. | \n \n \n| \n Pipeline | \n The Kanban board (Section 7). | \n \n \n| \n Candidates | \n \n Flat list of every candidate linked to this job, with a live search box that filters by\n name, title, company, source or email as you type.\n | \n \n \n| \n Interviews | \n Sessions for this req: schedule, copy invite links, watch status, open reports. | \n \n \n| \n Anti-Ghost | \n Pipeline health score, stale-candidate and no-show alerts, nurture settings. | \n \n \n \n Tip The header of each candidate row shows their match score pill. Bands: 80+\n (strong), 60–79 (good), below 60 (stretch). A dash means not scored yet.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 5. The Ideal Candidate Profile (ICP) \n \n The ICP is the contract between you and the sourcing/screening agents. Time invested here pays\n back across the entire pipeline.\n \n \n### What the ICP contains \n \n \n- Must-have skills and nice-to-have skills (chips you can add/remove). \n \n- Seniority & years of experience ranges. \n \n- Certifications required or preferred. \n \n- Disqualifiers — hard "no" criteria the screener enforces. \n \n- \n Location preference — a first-class field. If you clear it, it means "no location\n preference" (Lexy will not silently fall back to the job\'s address). Out-of-area\n candidates are kept but flagged, never hidden.\n \n \n \n### Editing the ICP \n \n \n- Open Work Order → ICP . Each section renders as editable chips. \n \n- Click a chip to remove it; use the add field to insert new criteria. \n \n- \n Changes save against the latest ICP version — edits are immediate and used by the very next\n sourcing or screening run.\n \n \n \n Who can edit Recruiters can edit the ICP of reqs assigned to them. On unassigned reqs,\n ICP changes are admin-only.\n \n \n Tip for remote roles Set the job\'s work type to remote — external sourcing will\n then search without any location constraint. For located roles, sourcing automatically widens\n city → region → country if the exact city returns nothing, and labels each result with the\n tier it came from.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 6. Sourcing & AI Agent Runs \n \n### Internal first \n \n Lexy always looks at your own bench before spending on external search. External sourcing only\n unlocks after the internal review step is completed for the req — this is enforced by the\n platform, not just suggested.\n \n \n### Starting a run \n \n \n- \n From the Work Order\'s Sourcing tab (or the dashboard Command Center), click\n Run Sourcing .\n \n \n- \n If a run is already in progress for that job, Lexy opens the existing run instead of\n starting a duplicate.\n \n \n- \n Watch progress live: each step (ICP check, internal search, external providers, scoring,\n dedup) streams as events.\n \n \n \n### What a run produces \n \n \n- \n A ranked list of sourced candidates with match scores, source labels (internal bench, PDL,\n web search) and a location-tier label for external results.\n \n \n- \n Automatic deduplication — one candidate record per person per tenant, keyed by email. If a\n sourced person matches an existing record you\'ll be prompted to merge rather than creating a\n duplicate.\n \n \n- \n New candidates land in the Sourced lane of the pipeline and are automatically\n resume-screened when a resume is available.\n \n \n \n### Platform Recommendations \n \n If you opt a job in (Sourcing tab toggle), Lexy\'s platform pool can push consenting,\n privacy-screened candidates into your pipeline. Candidates control their own discoverability;\n you only ever see people who opted in.\n \n \n### Agent Hub & AI Job Queue \n \n \n- \n Agent Hub shows each agent\'s recent runs, success rates and lets you trigger "Run\n now".\n \n \n- \n AI Job Queue lists queued background AI tasks (screenings, rescores, enrichments) and\n their statuses. Duplicate work is automatically collapsed.\n \n \n- \n Runs interrupted by a platform restart are labeled interrupted , not failed — just\n re-run them.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 7. The Pipeline Board (Kanban) \n The Pipeline tab is where you move people through the hiring flow. \n \n### Lanes \n \n Working lanes follow the typical flow\n Sourced → Screened/Verified → Outreach → Interview stages → Offer stages → Hired . Exact\n lane names on your board may vary slightly by workspace configuration (for example,\n verification and hiring-manager review may appear as their own lanes). Terminal stages don\'t\n clutter the board:\n \n \n \n- Hired candidates appear in a celebratory wins strip. \n \n- \n Rejected / withdrawn / closed candidates live in the Closed drawer — open it\n to review or Restore someone back into a working lane.\n \n \n \n### Cards \n \n \n- \n Each card shows name, current title/company, match score pill, and status badges (screening\n verdict, verification flag, interview state).\n \n \n- \n Copy interview link right from the card once a session exists — the link is the exact\n magic link the candidate uses. If your browser blocks the clipboard, Lexy shows the link in\n a prompt for manual copy.\n \n \n- \n Action buttons advance the offer funnel (offer extended, accepted, declined) and record\n outcomes for analytics.\n \n \n \n### Moving candidates \n \n \n- Drag a card between lanes, or use the stage menu on the card. \n \n- \n Your manual move always wins. If an agent gate would normally hold a candidate (e.g.\n verification pending before outreach), an explicit recruiter move overrides it.\n \n \n- \n Moving into Interview can trigger the interview invitation flow; moving into\n Rejected can trigger a brand-voice rejection email.\n \n \n- \n Need a silent move (data cleanup, recording history)? Use “skip automation” in the\n move dialog — the candidate changes stage with no emails, invites, or agent runs\n fired.\n \n \n \n### Stage automation summary \n \n \n| \n Entering stage | \n What Lexy does automatically | \n \n \n| \n Sourced / linked to job | \n Resume screening runs (if a resume exists); match score computed. | \n \n \n| \n Verify | \n Verification agent runs for every candidate entering the stage. | \n \n \n| \n Outreach | \n Outreach agent drafts a personalized email → waits in your approval queue. | \n \n \n| \n Interview | \n Interview invitation (magic link) can be generated and sent. | \n \n \n| \n Rejected | \n AI-written, brand-voice rejection email (with a safe template fallback). | \n \n \n \n Positive replies auto-advance When a sourced candidate replies positively to outreach,\n Lexy classifies the reply and can advance them to Interview automatically, sending the\n interview invite in the same motion.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 8. Candidates & the 360° Profile \n \n### The Candidates list \n \n \n- \n Your full visible bench, grouped into Matched (has accrued intelligence) and\n Unmatched .\n \n \n- Filters for stage, source, activity. "Active" is derived from real recent activity. \n \n- \n Erased (GDPR) and do-not-contact candidates are excluded everywhere — lists, counts and\n analytics alike.\n \n \n \n### The 360° profile \n \n \n| \n Area | \n Details | \n \n \n| \n Header | \n \n Name, title, company, contact info, Fit Score ring (0–100 hire probability),\n current stage, trust/verification badge.\n | \n \n \n| \n Intelligence | \n \n The accrued multi-dimension score (technical, domain, trajectory, engagement, and more).\n Dimensions not yet evidenced show — . This accrued score is the source of\n truth on every surface — point-in-time match scores are only a fallback.\n | \n \n \n| \n Resume Screening | \n \n Extracted work history, matched vs. missing skills, AI recommendation and reasoning.\n | \n \n \n| \n Interviews | \n \n Every session: recording player, per-question grades, transcript, proctoring summary.\n | \n \n \n| \n Verification | \n \n Identity/employment consistency results and any flags. The badge appears only when a real\n verification result exists.\n | \n \n \n| \n Timeline | \n \n Chronological event feed: stage changes, emails sent/received, interviews, notes, outcome\n events.\n | \n \n \n| \n Connection strength | \n \n An engagement score that only grows through real completed interactions. A zero is honest\n — it means no completed engagement yet, not an error.\n | \n \n \n \n Trust gate When a candidate\'s trust score is low or unverified, primary surfaces lead\n with the gate badge so you see the caveat before the score.\n \n \n### Adding candidates manually \n \n \n- \n Add candidate — form entry; if the email matches an existing record you\'ll get a\n merge prompt instead of a duplicate.\n \n \n- \n Bulk import — CSV/spreadsheet upload; supports flagging rows as current employees for\n the internal-mobility bench.\n \n \n- \n Parse CVs — drop resumes; Lexy extracts profiles and links them to the job (only on\n approved jobs).\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 9. Resume Screening & Verification \n \n### Resume screening \n \n \n- \n Runs automatically whenever a candidate with a resume is linked to a job — sourced, imported\n or manually added.\n \n \n- \n Produces: recommendation (advance / review / reject), matched skills, missing skills,\n summary, and evidence quotes.\n \n \n- \n Skills found in the resume are merged into the candidate\'s skill set, and the match score is\n recomputed after enrichment.\n \n \n- \n The screening verdict drives the default Kanban lane — but your manual placement always\n overrides it, and a human rejection is never overwritten by a re-screen.\n \n \n \n### Fairness by construction \n \n What the AI never sees Every AI scorer runs behind a fairness firewall: personally\n identifying details (name, photo, contact info, demographic hints) are redacted before\n scoring, and every scoring prompt carries a fairness directive. Candidates with sparse\n profiles are scored on the skills they show — absence of a job title is not treated as a\n mismatch.\n \n \n### Verification \n \n \n- Runs automatically for every candidate entering the Verify stage. \n \n- \n Checks profile consistency (employment claims, public footprint) and produces a verdict with\n flags.\n \n \n- \n While it runs, the profile shows a live "verifying…" indicator; the badge appears only when\n a real result lands.\n \n \n- A pending verification never blocks you: an explicit stage move overrides the gate. \n \n\n \n \n\n## 10. Outreach, Approvals & the Inbox \n \n### How outreach works \n \n \n- A candidate enters the Outreach stage (or you enroll them in a sequence). \n \n- \n The Outreach Agent writes a personalized email using your tenant\'s brand voice, documents\n and the job context.\n \n \n- \n The draft lands in Pending approvals . Nothing sends without you (unless your admin\n has explicitly enabled autopilot for a campaign).\n \n \n \n### Reviewing drafts \n \n \n- \n Open Outreach → Pending . Each draft shows the candidate, job, subject and body.\n \n \n- Edit in place — click into subject or body, adjust, and save. Then approve. \n \n- Approve queues the send; Discard drops the draft. \n \n- \n A candidate with no usable email can\'t be approved — the "no email on file" gate is\n non-overridable; add an email to the profile first.\n \n \n \n### Sequences & campaigns \n \n \n- \n Build multi-step sequences with delays and A/B subject variants in the Campaign Manager.\n \n \n- Step messages honor the same approval rules; edits are per-message. \n \n- Every send is deduplicated — a candidate never receives the same first touch twice. \n \n \n### The Inbox \n \n \n- \n Replies flow into a shared, tenant-wide inbox — every reply is captured even if a req has no\n assigned recruiter.\n \n \n- \n The Conversation Agent classifies each reply: Interested , Not now ,\n Question , Unsubscribe .\n \n \n- \n Interested replies can auto-advance the candidate to Interview and trigger the\n invite.\n \n \n- \n Unsubscribe adds the candidate to the Do-Not-Contact list immediately; DNC is\n enforced platform-wide.\n \n \n- \n Where your tenant uses Microsoft 365, replies to recruiter mailboxes sync into Lexy\n automatically.\n \n \n \n Kill switch Admins have a tenant-wide kill switch that halts every AI-generated message\n instantly — use it if anything ever looks wrong with automated sending.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 11. AI Interviews (end to end) \n \n Lexy conducts live, voice-based structured interviews. The interviewer is always "Lexy" — a\n consistent, calibrated persona.\n \n \n### Interview types \n \n \n- Screening interview — role-based structured screen for a specific work order. \n \n- Technical interview — includes coding/answer submissions where configured. \n \n- \n Mock & baseline interviews — candidate-initiated practice from their portal\n (results visible to the candidate only).\n \n \n \n### Inviting a candidate \n \n \n- \n From the pipeline card, candidate profile, or Work Order → Interviews, choose\n Invite to interview .\n \n \n- \n Lexy generates a magic link — a private URL that is itself the candidate\'s\n credential. No account or password needed.\n \n \n- \n Send it via the built-in email, or click Copy link on the pipeline card to share it\n yourself.\n \n \n- \n When you generate a link yourself, re-clicking reuses the existing session rather than\n creating a duplicate. (Invites triggered automatically by a positive outreach reply create\n their own fresh session.)\n \n \n \n Approval gate applies Interview links only work on approved work orders. If a job is\n pushed back to pending/rejected, existing links stop working until it\'s re-approved.\n \n \n### Directing the interview \n \n \n- \n In the Work Order\'s interview settings you can set a focus directive ("probe system\n design depth") and add custom questions for all interview types.\n \n \n- \n Custom questions are guaranteed to be asked verbatim; they replace some of the generated\n questions so total length stays the same.\n \n \n- Defaults can be set once per job and apply to every session created after. \n \n \n### What the candidate experiences \n \n \n- \n Opens the magic link → sees the start screen with the job context and, if configured,\n a personal video message from you (Section 12).\n \n \n- \n Gives explicit consent to AI interviewing and recording — the interview cannot start without\n it, and revoking mid-interview halts all capture instantly.\n \n \n- \n Grants mic/camera access. Lexy speaks each question aloud; the candidate answers naturally\n by voice. Works on desktop and mobile, in multiple languages (the session language follows\n the invite).\n \n \n- \n Long answers are safe: Lexy waits while the candidate is actively speaking and never cuts\n off mid-thought.\n \n \n- \n Lexy closes the interview gracefully when the conversation reaches a natural farewell.\n \n \n \n### After the interview \n \n \n- \n Per-question grades — each answer is scored once at completion with reasoning;\n ungraded items show — , and a genuine 0 shows as 0.\n \n \n- \n Summary & overall score , competency breakdown (calibrated so competency averages\n can\'t inflate above the graded overall).\n \n \n- Recording — full audio/video playback in the candidate profile. \n \n- \n Proctoring signals — face presence, gaze, tab switches; the risk level, flags and\n notes always agree with the same per-signal thresholds shown in the UI.\n \n \n- \n Work authorization — asked as a separate non-scored step, stored as compliance data,\n never fed to the scorer.\n \n \n- \n On completion the candidate is automatically advanced past the Interview stage in your\n pipeline.\n \n \n- \n No-shows — an overdue scheduled interview flips to No show automatically and\n notifies the req owner; Anti-Ghost can nurture from there.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 12. Recruiter Intro Videos \n \n Put a human face on the process: candidates see "A message from your recruiter" before their\n interview starts.\n \n \n \n- Go to Settings → Intro Video (or your profile settings). \n \n- \n Upload a photo of yourself and pick a voice/tone. Lexy generates a short, personalized\n avatar video (per language, cached and reused).\n \n \n- Preview the script first, tweak the tone, then generate. \n \n- \n Every interview invite for your reqs now shows your video on the candidate\'s start screen.\n If generation is unavailable, candidates see a branded Lexy fallback — the interview is\n never blocked.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 13. Evaluation Reports & Hiring-Manager Sharing \n \n### The Candidate Evaluation Report \n \n \n- \n A client-facing report for a specific candidate × role: profile summary, match analysis,\n interview assessment, verification status, recommendation.\n \n \n- \n Generated automatically the first time you export; it carries a\n draft notice until you approve it . Approve once you\'ve reviewed — subsequent exports\n drop the notice.\n \n \n- \n Export as PDF from the candidate page, the interview page, or attach it when sharing with a\n hiring manager — these surfaces use the same evaluation report (a simpler legacy export\n exists as a fallback in rare cases).\n \n \n \n### Sharing with a Hiring Manager (no login needed) \n \n \n- From the candidate profile choose Share with hiring manager . \n \n- \n Lexy creates a private, expiring link containing a sanitized snapshot: evaluation, resume,\n interview highlights. No login required — the link itself is the credential; treat it like a\n confidential document.\n \n \n- \n The HM can record a decision (advance / reject / discuss) and leave feedback directly in the\n page.\n \n \n- Their decision and comments land in your inbox and on the candidate\'s timeline. \n \n \n Attachments open correctly Resumes attach in their true format (PDF or Word) — Lexy\n detects the file type so hiring managers never receive an unopenable file.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 14. Talent Match, Rediscovery & Internal Talent \n \n### Talent Match \n \n \n- \n On a candidate: see every role they fit across your visible reqs, with per-role fit scores.\n \n \n- On a job: see the best matches from your existing bench before sourcing externally. \n \n- \n Scores are computed against the job\'s context; where no stored score exists yet, a\n deterministic signal-based estimate is shown (never a random number).\n \n \n \n### Talent Rediscovery \n \n \n- \n Surfaces past candidates (silver medalists, previous applicants) who now match a new req.\n \n \n- \n Reading/rediscovering is open across your agency; acting (linking to a req, outreach)\n requires the req to be assigned to you.\n \n \n \n### Internal Talent \n \n \n- \n A dedicated internal-mobility search over your own employees and bench (marked via import or\n the employee toggle on a profile).\n \n \n- \n Strictly firewalled to your tenant pool — internal search never mixes in external or\n platform candidates.\n \n \n- \n This is also the "internal first" step that unlocks external sourcing spend (Section 6).\n \n \n \n### Staleness — fair but honest \n \n Long-inactive candidates gently rank lower in match lists (never hidden, scores never\n rewritten). Lexy also runs a 6-month check-in program that emails quiet candidates asking them\n to refresh their status; self-reported job changes re-engage them automatically.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 15. Engagement & Anti-Ghost \n \n### Engagement \n \n \n- \n Tracks candidate interest signals: email opens/replies, portal activity, interview\n completion.\n \n \n- \n Feeds the connection-strength score on each profile (only real completed events count).\n \n \n \n### Anti-Ghost \n \n \n- \n Pipeline Health per work order: a score with the specific candidates dragging it\n down.\n \n \n- \n Alerts for: no replies after N touches, interview no-shows, stale in-stage candidates.\n \n \n- \n Nurture actions: schedule a follow-up touch (goes through the same approval flow), or hand\n back to you with a suggested next step.\n \n \n- Candidate status check-ins keep long-term bench data fresh automatically. \n \n\n \n \n\n## 16. Analytics, Calibration & Fairness \n \n### Hiring analytics \n \n \n- \n Funnel — stage-to-stage conversion for your reqs, split by how candidates entered\n (sourced vs. applied).\n \n \n- Source quality — hire-rate and progression by source. \n \n- Outcomes — offers extended/accepted/declined, time-to-hire. \n \n- \n All analytics respect the same compliance filters as your lists (erased/DNC candidates are\n excluded and labeled as such).\n \n \n \n### AI calibration \n \n \n- \n Override rate — how often your team disagrees with AI recommendations, per agent.\n \n \n- \n Learning insights — where the AI\'s scoring is drifting from your actual decisions,\n with suggested adjustments.\n \n \n- \n Per-tenant learned scoring only ever activates after enough evidence and after\n beating the baseline in a backtest — otherwise Lexy stays on defaults.\n \n \n \n### Fairness monitoring \n \n \n- \n Adverse-impact monitoring (4/5ths rule) over stage progression, computed on anonymized\n aggregates.\n \n \n- \n Demographics are firewalled from all scoring; they exist only in aggregate fairness views.\n \n \n- Sourcing diversity views are k-anonymized — no individual is ever identifiable. \n \n\n \n \n\n## 17. Market Intelligence & Ask Lexy \n \n \n- Hiring Velocity — how fast similar roles are moving on the platform. \n \n- Candidate Supply — depth of available talent for a skill/region. \n \n- \n Comp Signal — salary expectation ranges, built only from cross-tenant aggregates\n (never individual records).\n \n \n- Internal Bench — your own availability before you buy externally. \n \n- \n Ask Lexy — a natural-language chat over these tools. Every answer cites its data\n source, and when there isn\'t enough data Lexy says "no data" rather than guessing.\n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 18. LINX Queue (agency ↔ client collaboration) \n \n \n- \n LINX lets a client tenant send staffing requests to your agency (and vice versa) without\n sharing full workspaces.\n \n \n- \n Incoming requests appear in the LINX Queue with the role details and requesting\n party.\n \n \n- \n Accept clones the request into a work order in your own tenant;\n Decline returns it with a reason.\n \n \n- Both sides can see the request status; only the originating side can withdraw it. \n \n\n \n \n\n## 19. Team, Settings & Subscription \n \n### Team (admins) \n \n \n- Invite teammates by email with a role; they activate via the invite link. \n \n- \n Edit roles — Recruiter Admins can manage line staff in their own tenant; only higher\n roles can promote to admin.\n \n \n- \n Assign work orders to recruiters — remember, assignment controls what a recruiter can see.\n \n \n- \n The member count reflects staff only (candidates with portal accounts are never counted as\n team members).\n \n \n \n### Settings \n \n \n- \n Brand & voice — company description, tone, documents. This context flavors every\n candidate-facing email Lexy writes, including rejections.\n \n \n- Intro video — your personal avatar video (Section 12). \n \n- Interview defaults — per-job focus directives and custom questions. \n \n- Notifications — email digests and reply alerts. \n \n- Theme — light/dark. \n \n \n### Subscription (tenant admins) \n \n \n- \n Country-based subscription with pricing per country; status moves automatically through\n active → grace → suspended based on paid-through date.\n \n \n- Recording a payment is the only manual step; everything else is automatic. \n \n\n \n \n\n## 20. Compliance, Privacy & Candidate Consent \n \n \n- \n Interview consent — candidates must explicitly consent before any AI interview\n capture; revocation stops recording, transcription and scoring immediately, mid-interview.\n \n \n- \n Do Not Contact — one unsubscribe anywhere blocks all future automated contact\n platform-wide.\n \n \n- \n Erasure (GDPR) — erased candidates vanish from every list, count, export and\n analytic.\n \n \n- \n Candidate privacy controls — platform-pool candidates control their discoverability;\n pausing hides them everywhere including from historical "viewed you" style surfaces.\n \n \n- \n Candidate-facing framing — candidates never see raw low scores; their portal shows\n percentile bands and growth guidance. What you see internally is more detailed than what\n they see.\n \n \n- \n EEO & work authorization — demographic questions are never asked in interviews;\n work-authorization capture is separate from scoring.\n \n \n- \n EU AI Act — Lexy maintains decision audit logs, deviation panels and documentation\n surfaces for regulated-market clients.\n \n \n- \n Data isolation — every tenant\'s data is isolated; agencies see their client\n sub-tenants only through explicit hierarchy, and recruiters see only assigned reqs.\n \n \n \n Your responsibilities Treat magic links and HM share links as confidential. Don\'t paste\n candidate PII into outside tools. Record real outcomes (offers, hires, rejections) —\n calibration and fairness monitoring depend on truthful data.\n \n\n \n \n\n## 21. Troubleshooting & FAQ \n \n \n| \n Symptom | \n Likely cause & fix | \n \n \n| \n "I can\'t see a candidate/work order I know exists." | \n The req isn\'t assigned to you. Ask your Recruiter Admin to assign it. | \n \n \n| \n "The interview link says the interview isn\'t available." | \n \n The work order isn\'t approved (or was pushed back). Approve it and the link works again.\n | \n \n \n| \n "Sourcing found nobody." | \n \n Location too narrow (Lexy auto-widens, but check the ICP location), or internal review not\n yet completed for external spend.\n | \n \n \n| \n "Outreach draft won\'t approve." | \n \n Candidate has no email on file — add one to the profile first. This gate cannot be\n overridden.\n | \n \n \n| \n "A score shows a dash." | \n \n Not evaluated yet — that\'s honest, not broken. Trigger the relevant step (screening,\n interview) to get a score.\n | \n \n \n| \n "Work Order Not Found on a job I just had open." | \n \n You\'re logged in as a different user in another tab. Log back in as yourself; visibility\n is per-user.\n | \n \n \n| \n "Copy link didn\'t copy." | \n \n Your browser blocked clipboard access; Lexy shows the link in a dialog — copy it manually.\n | \n \n \n| \n "Candidate says the interview froze." | \n Rare connectivity issue; the session is resumable — have them reopen the same link. | \n \n \n| \n "Duplicate candidate warning when adding." | \n \n A record with that email already exists. Choose merge — Lexy never creates duplicates by\n email.\n | \n \n \n\n \n \n\n## 22. Glossary \n \n \n| \n Term | \n Meaning | \n \n \n| \n Work Order | \n A hiring requisition/job, with its own pipeline, ICP, interviews and analytics. | \n \n \n| \n ICP | \n Ideal Candidate Profile — the editable criteria the AI sources and screens against. | \n \n \n| \n Magic link | \n A private interview URL that acts as the candidate\'s credential — no login needed. | \n \n \n| \n Match score | \n A point-in-time fit score for candidate × job (bands: 80+ / 60–79 / <60). | \n \n \n| \n Intelligence / accrued score | \n \n The continuously updated multi-dimension candidate score; the source of truth once it\n exists.\n | \n \n \n| \n Fit Score ring | \n The 0–100 hire-probability visual on the candidate profile header. | \n \n \n| \n DNC | \n Do Not Contact — a platform-wide block on automated contact. | \n \n \n| \n Sourced candidate | \n A person found by the Sourcing Agent, pending your engagement. | \n \n \n| \n Platform pool | \n Opt-in candidates discoverable across the platform, privacy-screened. | \n \n \n| \n Closed drawer | \n Where rejected/withdrawn candidates live off the board; restorable. | \n \n \n| \n Anti-Ghost | \n The agent + module that detects silence/no-shows and nurtures. | \n \n \n| \n HM share link | \n An expiring, no-login link giving a hiring manager a sanitized candidate package. | \n \n \n| \n LINX | \n Cross-tenant staffing request exchange between clients and agencies. | \n \n \n| \n Morning Report | \n Your daily digest of agent activity and priorities, with honest counts. | \n \n \n| \n Proctoring | \n Interview integrity signals: face presence, gaze, tab switches. | \n \n \n\n \n © 2026 Lexy AI • This guide reflects the platform as of July 2026. Features may evolve — the\n in-app experience is always authoritative.';
